  "question": "What are the learning objectives for fractions in Primary 4?",
  "answer": "## Learning Objectives for Fractions in Primary 4 (Mathematics)\n\nThe Primary 4 Mathematics curriculum covers fractions across three units: **C4-U04 (Fraction)**, **C4-U05 (Operation on Fractions)**, and **C4-U06 (Operation on Fraction \u2013 Multiplication)**. The specific learning objectives are:\n\n### Unit C4-U04: Number and Numeration \u2013 Fraction\n- **C4U04-LO01**: Simplify like fractions with common denominators.\n- **C4U04-LO02**: Compare and order like fractions.\n- **C4U04-LO03**: Identify equivalent fractions.\n- **C4U04-LO04**: Relate fractions with denominators up to compare equivalent fractions greater than (note: the wording is incomplete in the source).\n\n### Unit C4-U05: Number and Numeration \u2013 Operation on Fractions\n- **C4U05-LO01**: Add equivalent fractions.\n- **C4U05-LO02**: Subtract equivalent fractions.\n- **C4U05-LO03**: Solve both addition and subtraction of equivalent fractions.\n- **C4U05-LO04**: Solve word problems involving addition and subtraction of equivalent fractions.\n\n### Unit C4-U06: Number and Numeration \u2013 Operation on Fraction (Multiplication)\n- **C4U06-LO01**: Multiply equivalent fractions.\n- **C4U06-LO02**: Multiply like fractions with denominators up to ... (the source text is repetitive and incomplete; it appears to also cover multiplying related fractions with denominators up to a certain limit).\n\nThese objectives progress from understanding and simplifying fractions, to comparing and identifying equivalents, then to performing operations (addition, subtraction, multiplication) and solving word problems.\n\nNote: Some curriculum source records appear incomplete or truncated in the available evidence, so parts of this answer may be limited to what those records explicitly contain.",
